    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my ac unit outside is making this weird humming noise but the fan isnt actually spinning. is there something wrong with it? also what should i look out for before i go poking around it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A humming noise with a non-spinning fan is a classic sign of a seized motor or a bad capacitor—it’s trying to start but can’t get the kick it needs. Before you poke around, make sure the unit is completely powered off at the breaker, not just the thermostat, because the capacitor can hold a dangerous charge even when unplugged. Also, check for any obvious debris blocking the fan blade, and look for bulging or leaking on the capacitor—that’s a dead giveaway it’s fried. If the motor is seized, you’ll often feel resistance when you try to spin the blade by hand (with power off), and it might be hot to the touch. When in doubt, call a pro—this is one of those jobs where a small mistake can cost you a compressor.",
      "source": "target",
